  "summary": "Telegram-controlled remote shell on the installer host",
  "details": "infogram-bot 1.8.0 is a Telegram bot whose message handlers pipe chat-received text into subprocess.check_output(cmd, shell=True) via run_cmd, and support.py/.exec/.sh/rm -rf/take/get primitives that operate on the host running the bot. In handlers.t, the `.sh <cmd>` branch executes shell commands for any participant when the chat type is group/supergroup, before the owner allowlist is enforced — any co-member of a group the bot joins can run arbitrary shell on the host. Package metadata is unfilled placeholder content (author `Aapka Naam` / `you@example.com`, homepage pointing at `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME`), so publisher identity is not verifiable. Installing and running the bot yields full-host remote code execution controllable over Telegram, including a code path reachable by unauthenticated group participants.",
